Subject: Tweak: training opponent
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

Training's opponent, the team nobody plays, no longer always vanishes but
the launcher chooses it.

Its captain is the launcher's (the title's StartTrainingMatch; Bowser, or
Mario against Bowser, when it is the same as the trainee's or not chosen);
its sidekicks stay those of its lineup in the save.

How many of its four fielders play is the launcher's too: cTeam::ResetCharacters
freezes all but that many in FROZEN_SHATTERED at every kickoff, the last
ones first, so the captain is the last to go.

Its goalie, a Kritter, can be taken out: Goalie::Update leaves it intangible
to the ball and the players, invisible, without a shadow and far from the
field, at every step, and does nothing else (a save would need the shot's
save data, which it never gets). By default it stays.

The side the player plays is the launcher's too: StartTrainingMatch puts the
captain and the pad on the home or the away side, and the opponent on the
other.

Its skill is the launcher's too (GameInfoManager::ApplyDifficultySettings gives
the team nobody plays the difficulty of that level of the game's skill
setting), by default the game's own.

A goal can go straight to the kickoff: Presentation::OnGoalScored takes the
way the game's own no_presentation setting does, which skips the
celebration and the replay. A mega strike's goal keeps its presentation. The
goal's other listener that matters, OnCharactersGoalScored, which takes the
players' pads away for the celebration, does the same as for that setting,
or the players would stay without them after the kickoff.

The same setting skips the match's introduction: FrontEnd::EnterStartScreen
begins the training match straight at the kickoff, as it does for the
Strikers 101 lessons.

